    skos:definition "Regular and systematic pattern of growth such that the mass or size of any organ or part of a body can be expressed in relation to the total mass or size of the entire organism according to the allometric equation: \\[Y = b{x^{\\alpha}}\\] where \\(Y\\) = mass of the organ, \\(x\\) = mass of the organism, \\(\\alpha\\) = growth coefficient of the organ, and \\(b\\) is a constant."@en ;
    skos:inScheme goldbook: ;
    skos:prefLabel "allometric growth"@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf goldbook: ;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.15455> ;
.

